Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── The morning's news ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At eight on the morning the book closes, what became of each of the city's people is told, as Sennet tells it,
  // wherever the company is in the city. In a world that goes on, the city goes on from it.
  Query newsHour() means closingDay() and hour(clock) == 8.
  Rule news_perrin_dead when newsHour() and perrinDead(party) once says "Of Perrin Halyard: the merfolk brought him up the Fish Stairs at dawn and laid him on the third step, above the plate, which nobody stopped them doing. His mother came down the chain for him herself. This time there is a body in the coffin." { }
  Rule news_perrin_up when newsHour() and perrinUp(party) and not perrinDead(party) once says "Of Perrin Halyard: he has taken a room over the Sounding Line, with his leg up on a stool, and is teaching Peg Arkle's potman Aenean, and is visited twice a day by his mother and his brother, separately, and every evening at the turn of the tide by a merfolk girl at the foot of the Fish Stairs, where he sits on the third step to talk to her with his bad leg in the sea." { }
  Rule news_perrin_under when newsHour() and not perrinUp(party) and not perrinDead(party) and not cloudgateFell(sennet_bay) once says "Of Perrin Halyard: he is dead, officially, and was let down on the third day, and is in an air-bell under the bay with his leg mending, reading drowned books by an Aenean lamp, and is, the merfolk say, the happiest dead man in the Whelm." { }
  Rule news_brothers when newsHour() and aubreyFreed(aubrey) once says "Of Aubrey Halyard: he has stopped drinking his father's brandy, and started drinking his own, which is worse brandy and less of it. He goes down the chain every evening. Cloudgate has noticed that he looks at the view." { }
  Rule news_aubrey_guilt when newsHour() and not aubreyFreed(aubrey) and not perrinDead(party) once says "Of Aubrey Halyard: he is still on the sofa in his rooms, with a bottle, believing what he believes. Nobody has told him otherwise." { }
  Rule news_imogen when newsHour() and imogenSorry(imogen) once says "Of the Dowager Lady Halyard: she has been seen on the Quay, in black, buying an eel pie from Old Bethan, which she did not eat, and asking the way to the Fish Stairs." { }
  Rule news_rector_taken when newsHour() and rectorTaken(quance) once says "Of the Rector: she is in the Watch-house on Fish Street, and the Courant has stopped printing Thresholds in the middle of Chapter Thirty-One." { }
  Rule news_rector_fled when newsHour() and rectorFled(quance) once says "Of the Rector: she was seen at first light walking up the coast road toward the downs alone, in an ordinary grey coat, with no chain, and nobody has seen her since. The House has found her study tidy and her desk empty except for a black case with four hollows in it, and a note, in violet ink: I DID NOT REVISE THIS." { }
  Rule news_rector_through when newsHour() and rectorThrough(quance) and firstThrough(party) once says "Of the Rector: she went through the Door of Doors after you, into everywhere, and did not come out again. Mr. Tench has written in his ledger: MAGISTRA I. QUANCE. OUT. And has left the column for In empty." { }
  Rule news_tolley when newsHour() and tolleyFriend(tolley) once says "Of Mr. Tolley: the Courant on Fish Street has bought the first three chapters of A Romance of the Sea, by Edwin Tolley, for four coin, and asked for more." { }
  Rule news_fabian_home when newsHour() and fabianHome(party) once says "Of Fabian Murrey: he has taken the portrait of his grandmother down from over the counter at Murrey's, and put it up again, a little lower, and begun the seventh edition again from the first page, in pencil." { }
  Rule news_fabian_beloved when newsHour() and beloved(fabian) once says "Of Fabian Murrey, also: the seventh edition, when it comes out, will have a dedication. He will not tell anyone what it says, which in Lamp Street is taken to mean everyone knows." { }
  Rule news_fabian_away when newsHour() and fabianWilling(fabian) and not fabianHome(party) and not fabianLost(party) once says "Of Fabian Murrey: the shop on Lamp Street is shut, with a card in the window in pencil: GONE THROUGH. BACK SOON. F.M." { }
  Rule news_fabian_lost when newsHour() and fabianLost(party) once says "Of Fabian Murrey: the shop on Lamp Street is shut. Nobody has taken the books out of the window." { }
  Rule news_fabian_stayed when newsHour() and not fabianWilling(fabian) once says "Of Fabian Murrey: he is behind the counter at Murrey's, correcting the commas in his grandmother's book." { }
  Rule news_bethan when newsHour() and bethanAtPeace(bethan) once says "Of Old Bethan: she is asleep behind her barrow on the Quay, in the sun, with her mouth open, and the harbour is stepping round her." { }
  Rule news_hapenny when newsHour() and hapennyShopped(hapenny) and not cloudgateFell(sennet_bay) once says "Of Ha'penny: she sits on the third step every morning with her cockles and a glass fish, which she shows to the harbour children, who have never seen a merfolk child so pleased with a thing she cannot eat." { }
  Rule news_admittance when newsHour() and admittanceLaughed(admittance) and stepTold(admittance) and not cloudgateFell(sennet_bay) once says "Of No Admittance and Mr. Pumphrey: they have met, at the third step, with the whole Quay watching, she in her crown in the water and he in his brass buttons on the step above with the Bylaws under his arm. Nobody heard what was said. When it was over he took a screwdriver out of his pocket and took the brass plate off the step, and gave it to her, and she took it down into the Whelm, where it is hung, they say, over the back door of the Guildhall, under the other sign." { }
  Rule news_prue when newsHour() and prueFriend(prue) and not madeSet(sennet_bay) once says "Of Prue Quickly: her furnace is roaring and she has had a new card printed for the tray of red glass: GENUINE PETALS OF THE ROSE. NOT REAL. ONE COIN. They sell twice as fast." { }
  Rule news_prue_cold when newsHour() and furnaceCold(glasshouse) once says "Of Prue Quickly: her furnace is cold, and she has gone to blow bottles for her cousin in a glass-house in another town, where nobody has heard of the Rose." { }
  Rule news_jem when newsHour() and jemFree(jem) once says "Of Jem Tuttle: he is Peg Arkle's potman at the Sounding Line, or Prue Quickly's stoker, and has not looked up once since he came down, and says it is the most beautiful thing in the world, the ground." { }
  Rule news_kittiwake when newsHour() and strikeSettled(sennet_bay) once says "Of the winch-gang: it has had its third, and Mother Kittiwake has chalked a new line under UP 5 COIN. DOWN FREE. NO DOGS on the slate on the basket rail: MERMAIDS BY ARRANGEMENT." { }
  Rule news_florian_changed when newsHour() and florianChanged(florian) once says "Of the Honourable Florian Mottram: he has given his cabinet of souvenirs to the Museum of the Tour, with a note asking Dr. Cole to send home anything that wants to go. Miss Sone has given notice to the Mottrams, and been taken on by Florian, as he puts it, as a friend." { }
  Rule news_florian when newsHour() and not florianChanged(florian) once says "Of the Honourable Florian Mottram: he has bought a print of the Door of Doors, opened, for his cabinet." { }
  Rule news_ember when newsHour() and emberHome(fire_land) once says "Of the ember: Cabinet Fourteen in the Museum of the Tour is empty, and Dr. Cole has left the label in it, and written under it in pencil: GONE HOME." { }
  Rule news_chert when newsHour() and travelsWith(chert, party) once says "Of Chert: he is on your boot, looking at a gull." { }
  Rule news_thursday when newsHour() and doorOpen(sennet_bay) once says "Of Thursday, the House's cat: Mr. Tench saw him go through the cat-flap of the tower door yesterday, as he always does, and come out an hour later with sand in his fur from a beach nobody in Sennet has ever seen. The first through the Door of Doors in two hundred years, Mr. Tench says, may not have been a person." { }
  Rule news_true_home when newsHour() and airHome(sennet_bay) once says "Of the North Wind: he has his petal back, and the wind off the sea at Sennet this morning is from the north, and warm." { }
  Rule news_true_rose when newsHour() and roseMade(sennet_bay) and not airHome(sennet_bay) once says "Of the Air petal: it is in the Rose, in the boss of the Door of Doors, with the other three, and the North Wind has not been told." { }
  Rule news_rector_free when newsHour() and rectorFree() and doorOpen(sennet_bay) and not rectorThrough(quance) once says "Of the Rector: she came up the tower stair from the Lanterns at midnight and found the Door of Doors open and the Grand Tour won, and sat down on the floor of the Nexus in her gown of four colours, and laughed for a long time. This morning she has given out that the Tour is won, magnificently, and is dictating the chapter about it; and has asked Mr. Tolley, very pleasantly, for the winner's name and lodging." { }
  Rule news_rector_unopened when newsHour() and rectorFree() and not doorOpen(sennet_bay) and not cloudgateFell(sennet_bay) once says "Of the Rector: she is in her study, dictating, and has asked Mr. Tolley to find out where you are lodging." { }

  // ── In a world that goes on ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe after_market at glass_market when closingDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and doorOpen(sennet_bay) "In the Glass Market a hawker is selling prints of the Door of Doors, opened, at a penny, with a figure going through it whose face is left blank, so that the buyer can draw their own.".
  Observe after_quay at quay when closingDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and cloudgateFell(sennet_bay) "Halyard Hill stands in the bay a hundred yards off the end of the Fish Stairs, wet to its first floors, an island, with a ferry going out to it.".
  Observe after_crier at glass_market when closingDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and not doorOpen(sennet_bay) "The crier's board says THE GRAND TOUR CONTINUES, in red, and under it, in chalk, someone has written: WHO WITH?".
}
